-- glycerol again, now in the setting layer, which shows the medium case and the timescale case to be one
-- test with two clauses rather than two separate stories. Glycerol has exactly one operation on its
-- carbon-bound hydrogens: the exchange of its two arms, which is improper. It is not slow -- there is no
-- rate to be slow, since nothing performs it in time -- so it is recorded as fast and improper, and the
-- achiral clause of the admission test decides it.
glc-motions : List Motion
glc-motions = cons (nat-xch (cons 0 (cons 1 (cons 2 (cons 3 (cons 4 nil))))) (cons 9 (cons 10 (cons 11 (cons 12 (cons 13 nil))))) , 12 , false) nil
